  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1020 PM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nSfc gradient tightens on Saturday ahead of the next wave with\ngusty winds locally raising grassland fire weather concerns. Cloud\ncover will likely increase which will temper the warm up Saturday\nafternoon. The fast moving wave will sweep a cold front across the\nlocal region Saturday night. Moisture return will be brief but\nlikely sufficient to promote scattered showers ahead of the front\nSaturday night primarily across far E OK into NW AR. The western\nextent of the expanding instability axis will briefly be across\nthe region and an isolated thunderstorm could develop before\nfocusing more east. Any rainfall amounts will be light. \n\nCooler temperatures on Sunday with the pattern quickly resetting\non Monday beneath fast zonal flow aloft. This will allow southerly\nwinds to return and become gusty at times while temperatures trend\nwarmer mid to late week. A stronger wave may begin to impact the\nregion by late next week toward the end of this forecast period.",
